customer: nice_lady
problem: hamster
brief:
	Her child's hamster crept into the computer and lies on the fan. The symptoms are the Skater's (Dust Overheat) on purpose: the player finds the difference by opening it. The fan is fine; swapping it changes nothing.

== drop-off
(neutral) Hello, sir.
- Welcome to Compufun! How can I help you?
	(problem) I'm not sure you can help me, but I have an odd problem with my computer. As you can probably tell, it has started to smell terribly.
- Woha! What is that smell?
	(problem) I was hoping you could tell me!

- I'll [cough] take a [cough] look.
	(happy) Lovely! I'll check back later, I have some family issues to take care of for now.
	- [Cough] I'll call you when it's ready for pickup!
		(neutral) Thank you, sir. Goodbye!

== pick-up
(neutral) Hello, sir! That was quick!
- I have indeed found the issue and fixed it.
	(happy) That's just lovely!
- I have both good and bad news for you.
	(problem) Oh, no. That doesn't sound good. I'm still struggling with our family issues and now this.
	- I'm sorry to hear that...
	- I'll start with the good news then.
	- I'll start with the bad news then.
	(problem) Oh, god. Just tell me already.

- Just one little detail... There seems to have been a dead hamster in your chassi.
- Well... About that smell...
	(problem) Don't tell me something crawled up and died inside my computer because that's what it smelled like!
	- ...
(problem) Oh, no! Poor Mr Nibbles! So THAT'S where he went.
(neutral) Well, I guess I have two problems less to worry about. Thank you for your help. Goodbye sir.
